  "Question": "Groups A and B have the same mean. Group A has a standard deviation of 1.5, and Group B has a variance of 2. Which group has less variability (is more stable)? ( )",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Group A",
    "B": "Group B",
    "C": "Both groups are the same",
    "D": "Cannot be determined"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The variance of Group A is \\(1.5^2=2.25\\), which is greater than Group B's variance of 2. A smaller variance indicates greater stability, so Group B is more stable.",
